---
description: HOARDINGS360 performance rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# PERFORMANCE

Performance is a product requirement.

---

# SERVER FIRST

Prefer:

Server Components
server-side queries
server-side filtering
server-side pagination

Avoid unnecessary client fetching.

---

# DATABASE

Never fetch thousands of records just to filter them in React.

Bad:

SELECT *
then filter in browser.

Good:

database-side filtering + pagination.

---

# IMAGES

Use Next.js image optimization.

Do not load full-resolution images into thumbnails.

Lazy-load images when appropriate.

Use signed URLs for private buckets. Do not make buckets public to simplify thumbnails.

---

# CLIENT JAVASCRIPT

Avoid unnecessary:

useEffect
global state
large dependencies
client components

Do not turn entire pages into Client Components unnecessarily.

MapLibre, html5-qrcode, and qrcode must be loaded only on screens that need them.

---

# MAPS

Maps should not block the entire page.

Load expensive map functionality only when needed.

---

# PERFORMANCE REGRESSION

When implementing a feature, consider:

database query count
payload size
bundle size
image size
rendering cost
mobile network performance
